\section{Caveats}{
\itemize{
\item Benjamini-Hochberg controls the false discovery rate among the features tested. It is not a target-decoy q-value for identifications.
\item m is the number of finite p-values. Leave a line blank, or write NA, for a feature that was not tested rather than writing 1, which would enlarge the family.
\item stats fit already reports bh_adjusted per coefficient; use this verb for p-values from anywhere else.
}
}
\section{Performance}{
